    "post_rendered": "A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041cdaae1e0374a57abfbab28996bb87bf2bd933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3n + 1) \\times (3n + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" > table <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a1c6a6fbb477ff67f0d7dd55cb00169cb6b7ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n \\in \\mathbb{N})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" > is given. Prove that deleting any one of its squares yields a shape cuttable into pieces of the following form and its rotations: ''L&quot; shape formed by cutting one square from a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\"  width=\"40\" height=\"12\" > squares.",
    "post_canonical": "A $(3n + 1) \\times (3n + 1)$ table $(n \\in \\mathbb{N})$ is given. Prove that deleting any one of its squares yields a shape cuttable into pieces of the following form and its rotations: ''L\" shape formed by cutting one square from a $2 \\times 2$ squares.",
